  "id": "Compound::DB00470 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Dronabinol is shown to bind to Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the oxidation of various substrates, including quinones and other aromatic compounds. This binding leads to Cyp2c9 participating in oxidoreductive activities, which are then associated with Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Dronabinol influences Cyp3a4 through its interaction with Cyp2c9, which in turn affects the metabolic activity of Cyp3a4. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, with varying levels of confidence in the pathway strength. The presence of multiple pathways linking Dronabinol to Cyp3a4 through Cyp2c9 highlights a possible role in the metabolic processing of substrates, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Dronabinol and Cyp3a4, emphasizing the importance of Cyp2c9 in mediating this relationship.",
